<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmad Muadzam Shah of Pahang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1836–1914</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Wan Ahmad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmad al-Muadzam Shah, born Wan Ahmad, was ruler of Pahang on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malay-peninsula">Malay Peninsula</a>. He won the Pahang civil war of 1857–1863 against his brother Tun Mutahir, ruled as bendahara and in 1882 proclaimed himself sultan. In 1888 the British forced him to accept a resident, which provoked the Pahang uprising of 1891–1895.</p></div>
